---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<Base title="Our Team">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Our team" title="The people behind Navyug" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>
        Navyug Sanskriti Foundation is spearheaded by Vikram Singh, who has spent over a decade in this community — he
        began teaching for free in 2013, and went on to help run Vanphool Pathshala, a free school under the flyover
        reaching nearly 300 children by 2020, which was demolished by the Public Works Department in 2023 (<a href="https://thepatriot.in/reports/rising-from-the-rubble-33882">The Patriot</a>). Shrishti Verma, a lawyer who
        also taught at Vanphool Pathshala, handles NSF's legal and documentation work — critical for children who dropped out without records.
        Smitha Cunigal and Mihir Bhaskar have both spent several years managing government-partnered research at J-PAL
        and LEAD at Krea, and advise Navyug on fundraising and strategy.
      </p>

      <div class="person">
        <h3>Vikram Singh</h3>
        <div class="role">Co-Founder &amp; Executive Director</div>
        <p>
          Vikram holds an M.A. in Hindi (IGNOU, 2022), a B.Ed. (Chaudhary Ranveer Singh University, 2018), and a B.A.
          Hindi Honours (Delhi University, Maharaja Agrasen College, 2016). He began teaching for free in 2013 and
          went on to help run Vanphool Pathshala, a free school in Yamuna Khadar that by 2020 was running classes under
          the flyover and reaching nearly 300 children — and which was demolished by the Public Works Department in January 2023 (press coverage: <a href="https://thepatriot.in/reports/rising-from-the-rubble-33882">"Rising from the rubble", The Patriot</a>). He also taught at
          Manthan Coaching Centre (2016) and Lord Shiva Public School (2018), and led or contributed to social-research
          fieldwork with the Tata Institute of Social Sciences (TISS), the Institute of Social Studies Trust (ISST), and
          Jamia Millia Islamia (a study on Covid-19's impact on migrants and their children's education, sponsored by the
          National Human Rights Commission).
        </p>
        <p>
          In August 2020 he designed and managed a needs-assessment census of 1,500 households in Yamuna Khadar. His
          community organising track record includes running camps for voter ID, ration card, and Aadhaar applications;
          distributing ration kits during Covid-19 with Basti Suraksha Manch; running a temporary education centre for
          out-of-school children; and distributing mosquito nets and waterproof tarps ahead of monsoon season. He is
          fluent in Hindi and English.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="person">
        <h3>Shrishti Verma</h3>
        <div class="role">Co-Founder &amp; Head of Legal and Documentation</div>
        <p>
          Shrishti is a lawyer who also taught at Vanphool Pathshala. She is the Trust's Settlor/Founder of record and
          handles NSF's legal and compliance work — registration, certifications, and the documentation casework that is
          often the biggest barrier for children who have dropped out without records.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="person">
        <h3>Mihir Bhaskar</h3>
        <div class="role">Advisor, Fundraising &amp; Strategy</div>
        <p>
          Mihir has an M.S. in Public Policy &amp; Data Analytics from Carnegie Mellon (2021–23) and a B.A. in Economics
          from Cambridge (2013–16). He is a Senior Data Scientist at Stanford RegLab and previously spent four years at
          J-PAL South Asia (2017–2021), building an administrative-data research unit from 3 to 10 staff across 7
          projects and 3 states. He has separately run need-based relief efforts in the Mayur Vihar/Yamuna Khadar area
          since 2020, benefiting 660 families.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="person">
        <h3>Smitha Cunigal</h3>
        <div class="role">Advisor, Fundraising &amp; Strategy</div>
        <p>
          Smitha has 8 years of development and public-policy research experience in South Asia, most recently as
          Research Manager at J-PAL South Asia (2022–2024), where she managed government-partnered randomised evaluations
          — including one on personalised, level-based teaching in government schools — and managed grants up to USD
          976,000. She previously worked at LEAD at Krea (2017–2022) on financial-inclusion research.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
